# Pages follow DESIGN.md

Before writing or editing JSX in a page file, read [DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md).
It is the source of truth for all visual decisions and outranks both taste and
`AGENTS.md`. For a new page, follow the `new-page` skill
(`.cursor/skills/new-page/SKILL.md`) end to end.

Non-negotiables that generic Next.js/shadcn scaffolding violates:

- No card component, no shadow, no gradient. The one glow in the system belongs
  to the lit schedule window.
- Semantic tokens only — `text-chalk`, `text-silver`, `border-hairline`,
  `bg-bluehour`, `text-amber`, `font-display`. Never raw hex, never a warm grey.
- Amber `#ffb000` is light: at most one amber thing per screen region, marking
  the lit state or the primary action.
- 2px radius on interactive surfaces, 0 on rules, rails and panes.
- Groups of records are hairline-separated full-width rows
  (`border-b border-hairline py-9 first:border-t`), not a grid of boxes.
- Every band sits in `mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-5 py-16 sm:px-8`.
- No user-facing string in the file. Copy comes from `messages/{da,en,es}.json`
  via `getTranslations`, in sentence case; capitals come from `text-transform`.
- No `[locale]` segment in the route, and never `force-static`.
